    <h2>Awards</h2>
    <h3>Milano Photo Awards</h3>
    <h4>2026: 1st place in the category Portrait & Identity</h4>
    <p>
        <a href="https://www.instagram.com/p/DdpLya4Oj9i/" target="_blank">Link to the post.</a>
    </p>
    <p>'Part of “Deriva”, this photograph explores the unstable relationship between body, identity and social norms. The
        curled posture, hands gathered around the knees and sideways gaze suggest a tension between self-protection and
        exposure. Controlled light brings out the eyes and metallic details, while warm skin tones contrast with the cool
        backdrop. The curves of the body guide the viewer towards the face, creating an intimate composition despite the
        striking appearance. We awarded first place for its balance of visual impact, compositional precision and emotional
        ambiguity. The photograph holds our attention beyond its surface, turning the portrait into an exploration of
        vulnerability, control and the uncertain boundaries of identity.'</p>
